# Normalise line endings so the repo behaves identically on Windows, Linux and
# inside Docker builds.
#
# This matters here: Dockerfiles, shell snippets in CI, and `fly.toml` are all
# consumed by Linux tooling. If any of them were committed with CRLF, a Docker
# `RUN`/`CMD` or a bash step could fail with stray `\r` characters.
#
# `text=auto` detects text files, `eol=lf` stores *and* checks them out with LF,
# which removes any dependence on a contributor's `core.autocrlf` setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts should keep CRLF if any are ever added.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
